    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d97">

                <pb facs="0192" n="112" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg112"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bryan to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Petropolis, Brazil</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-08-05"><hi rendition="#italic">August 5,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 439.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my No. 438, I have the honor
                    to send herewith inclosed a copy of a letter just received from Mr. Jorge
                    Vereker, the American consular agent at Rio Grande do Sul, in which he reports
                    that the State authorities have ordered that proceedings against the firm of
                    Thomsen &amp; Co. be for the present suspended.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Page
                    Bryan.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d97-a1.xml" xpointer="d97-a1"/>
